  "review": {
    "result": "Independent core/store review found no actionable findings. Audio review identified redundant retained-plan and asset compilation. First-clock-only caching, per-clock asset grouping and exact intermediate translations address it; final review found no further runtime findings.",
    "added_evidence": [
      "80-clock journal caching, refusal/retry and distinct first-clock asset sets.",
      "Actual processed NTSC extent through nested Preserve and move/return clipping.",
      "Separate retained-edge and current coincident Hold endpoint regressions."
    ],
    "corrections": [
      "focused-sound-clock-1: removed unsupported ExactRatio ordering; positive original duration and equal placement lengths prove positivity.",
      "focused-sound-clock-2: selected the explicit AudioSample route type.",
      "focused-sound-clock-3: fixed plan fixture metadata comparisons and a shadowed fixture function.",
      "focused-sound-clock-4: repaired the short-occurrence fixture using a valid natural-rate SelectedPlacement.",
      "focused-sound-clock-5: corrected two mixed-bus suppression assertions. Suppression intersects all contributions; an independent route gap does not suppress an unmasked Original.",
      "focused-sound-clock-6: separated retained Automatic edge progress from current silent-Hold boundary ownership. A current exactly coincident Hold correctly uses its newly rounded endpoint.",
      "clippy-1: boxed the larger prepared-input enum variant.",
      "clippy-2: replaced a cloned singleton slice in the store regression with std::slice::from_ref.",
      "After clippy-2: updated the doctor capability and its assertion from schema-1-through-55 to schema-1-through-56 development-format refusal.",
      "workspace-1: the new gate fixture incorrectly expected a selected short input to have a shorter audible extent through Preserve. The corrected fixture owns its sound at the Retime output, bypassing its own processor and verifying the intended narrower audible range. Only routed_voice.rs changed after the broad run; its entire 11-test target was rerun."
    ]
  },
  "limits": [
    "Temporal transport is limited to an unchanged complete top-level sound-bearing processing branch through supported ordinary Sequence commands.",
    "Changed surviving branches, partial sound copies, copied retained clocks, root-owned temporal transport and unsupported occurrence isolation reject.",
    "Allowances, tails, native beat-sound placement and complete ib/ab semantics remain open.",
    "Preserve reference PCM uses the canonical DSP engine and does not independently qualify that algorithm.",
    "No optional app configuration, native GUI launch, acoustic, performance or emitted-movie checks in this increment.",
    "No full-product requirement or release gate is complete."
  ]
